#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198473 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198227 :question/id #uuid "a5637d71-22d4-548e-ad36-d09bff61d643" :question/math-academy-id "e-2398" :question/problem "Find the derivative of  $\\mathbf f(t) = \\langle \\sin t ,\\cos t , t \\rangle$ at $t= \\dfrac{\\pi}4.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find $\\mathbf f'(t)$ by differentiating each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute $\\mathbf f'\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}4\\right),$ we substitute $t=\\dfrac{\\pi}4$ into the expression for $\\mathbf f'(t)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right) & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right),\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right),\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\,-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b31f2bdc-c267-5fc7-bd0f-283777ee4fee" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050173 :topic/id #uuid "33e80361-ab74-58ae-9d96-655433239057" :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100859} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100860} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100861}] :topic/math-academy-id 1166 :topic/next [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048954} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049186} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049537} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050267}] :topic/title "Three-Dimensional Vectors in Component Form"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050420 :topic/difficulty 1.0 :topic/id #uuid "476d32c8-5b16-54ef-9688-daca6c7937ad" :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059675} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059676}] :topic/math-academy-id 280 :topic/next [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048813} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049070} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050902}] :topic/title "Differe