pe/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ \\pi  \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186578407} {:answer/id #uuid "f5c512e7-3fea-5b1f-9839-6c6d6cd76c5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ \\pi \\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186578664}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "49ea02f8-f7a5-5a9f-b433-d80c0119ee12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -\\pi \\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186578391} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc00062a-3083-5c1d-8f12-26ccb44d9639" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186578774}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7ef7fc1a-d9d2-557d-9621-842fb4ba0f43" :question/math-academy-id "q-130407" :question/problem "Find the derivative of  $f(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}{t}^{2}+3t \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t\\end{bmatrix}$ at $t=1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${f}^{′}(t)$ by differentiating each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}+3t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2t+3 \\\\ \\frac{1}{t} \\\\ \\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute ${f}^{′}(1)$ we substitute $t=1$ into the expression for ${f}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1) & =\\begin{bmatrix}2(1)+3 \\\\ \\frac{1}{1} \\\\ \\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi \\cdot 1)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2+3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ \\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi \\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -\\pi \\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186578882 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e27f6d2-73f0-58ef-832e-9344a0b38e26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/m