rac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(7t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-1,\\,7⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute ${f}^{′}(\\pi ),$ we substitute $t=\\pi$ into the expression for ${f}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(\\pi ) & =⟨-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi ),\\,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )-1,\\,7⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,-4,\\,7⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186616180 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a7f845c-40da-58cd-96ea-d2373cc5e194" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t \\\\ \\sqrt{6}{t}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t-7}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615588} {:answer/id #uuid "0fa5cace-431f-5c33-9900-ce3afb213a54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t \\\\ 2\\sqrt{6}t \\\\ \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t+7}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615594} {:answer/id #uuid "1c21e048-bd8a-598f-a73c-23089415fe3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t \\\\ \\sqrt{6}t \\\\ \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t-7}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615616} {:answer/id #uuid "5f28e3d2-5d4c-5b3a-a2e2-9c8ddcce8941" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t \\\\ 2\\sqrt{6}t \\\\ \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t-7}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615730} {:answer/id #uuid "ef9563f4-a4e8-5c10-9e0a-d12743257c85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t \\\\ 2\\sqrt{6}t \\\\ \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t+7}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615999}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f28e3d2-5d4c-5b3a-a2e2-9c8ddcce8941" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t \\\\ 2\\sqrt{6}t \\\\ \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t-7}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615730} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e4fea4e-a4d0-5d57-8a2e-bb25fe8a1ef5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616029}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9a6d01e0-8740-5c68-af20-18c404dc8b26" :question/math-academy-id "q-32419" :question/problem "Calculate the derivative of  $f(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t \\\\ \\sqrt{6}{t}^{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{t-7}\\end{bmatrix}$ with respect to $t.$" :question/worked-solution "We find ${f}^{′}(t)$ by differentiating each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{6}{t}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{t-7})\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t \\\\ 2\\sqrt{6}t \\\\ \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t-7}}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707884 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f8b7ac8d-9ece-5c77-a82f-ff8f6a0e6dd2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707892}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8b7ac8d-9ece-5c77-a82f-ff8f6a0e6dd2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707892} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a5ec290-59bf-5ccd-a606-9914dc58ab94" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707876} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e60fcf87-6e8c-5ee1-98b0-ee1bcb73c0cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707890}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e60fcf87-6e8c-5ee1-98b0-ee1bcb73c0cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707890} :answer-field/id #uuid "4306f823-242c-5636-842d-10fb9bbceedc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707879} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b6a54fdc-6925-52ab-b3a2-00c4cb6db02a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707887}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b6a54fdc-6925-52ab-b3a2-00c4cb6db02a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707887} :answer-field/id #uuid "faec65d0-bd53-57d1-a732-5689160ca82f" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707893}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "884e5745-5b1a-54cd-8919-ff8ecff31839" :question/problem "Given that $\\mathbf{f}(t)=\\langle 2\\cos t,\\,3\\sin t-t,\\,t^2\\rangle$, what is $\\mathbf{f}\\prime\\!\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)$?\n\n$\\mathbf{f}\\prime\\!\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)=\\langle$ {{field-1}} $,$ {{field-2}} $,$ {{field-3}} $\\rangle$" :question/worked-solution "First differentiate each component:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{f}\\prime(t)=\\left\\langle -2\\sin t,\\,3\\cos t-1,\\,2t\\right\\rangle.\n$$\n\nNow substitute $t=\\frac{\\pi}{2}$ into the derivative, using $\\sin\\!\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)=1$ and $\\cos\\!\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)=0$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{f}\\prime\\!\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)\n&=\\left\\langle -2(1),\\,3(0)-1,\\,2\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)\\right\\rangle \\\\\n&=\\langle -2,\\,-1,\\,\\pi\\rangle.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707886 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2668fd69-ac59-5eed-b886-d40e06cbbcf3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}t^2+2 \\\\ -\\sin t \\\\ e^t\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707875} {:answer/id #uuid "2e478991-09f9-5a62-875a-856836946ec1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3t^2+2 \\\\ \\sin t \\\\ e^t\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707877} {:answer/id #uuid "48878033-bcf8-52e2-b831-e84f43584d07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3t^2+2 \\\\ -\\sin t \\\\ e^t\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707880} {:answer/id #uuid "8db2051f-03ae-542d-9270-4258fb1d965a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3t^2+2 \\\\ \\cos t \\\\ e^t\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707885} {:answer/id #uuid "bd8f88ad-7262-53ef-a01c-31b6d6c35c3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3t^2+2 \\\\ -\\sin t \\\\ te^t\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707888}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "48878033-bcf8-52e2-b831-e84f43584d07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3t^2+2 \\\\ -\\sin t \\\\ e^t\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707880} :answer-field/id #uuid "1343331b-7380-5a71-a0ad-6e26953eed59" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707874}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a85e330d-0910-52bb-a13b-695bd7cb23d4" :question/problem "Calculate $\\mathbf{f}\\prime(t)$ given that $\\mathbf{f}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}t^3+2t \\\\ \\cos t \\\\ e^t\\end{bmatrix}$." :question/worked-solution "Differentiate each component separately, keeping the component order:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{f}\\prime(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{d}}{{dt}}(t^3+2t) \\\\ \\frac{{d}}{{dt}}(\\cos t) \\\\ \\frac{{d}}{{dt}}(e^t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3t^2+2 \\\\ -\\sin t \\\\ e^t\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe polynomial uses the power and sum rules, the derivative of $\\cos t$ is $-\\sin t$, and the derivative of $e^t$ is $e^t$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707891 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0efb5a37-edc5-5b0c-b21a-8f0d18da9f89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(\\arctan 2+\\frac{1}{5}\\right)\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{j}+\\cos 1\\,\\mathbf{k}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707873} {:answer/id #uuid "41b4faa0-b9de-5bf2-9692-bd3f0ea6f9e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(\\arctan 2+\\frac{2}{5}\\right)\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{j}+\\cos 1\\,\\mathbf{k}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707878} {:answer/id #uuid "67bfab15-8387-5877-9767-626add75c4d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\arctan 2\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{j}+\\cos 1\\,\\mathbf{k}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707882} {:answer/id #uuid "7656875b-ddb3-5bdc-89cf-66bd3665838c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(\\arctan 2+\\frac{2}{5}\\right)\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{j}-\\cos 1\\,\\mathbf{k}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707883} {:answer/id #uuid "da212d36-ee7c-58a6-8f46-aabc1184643a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(\\arctan 2+\\frac{2}{5}\\right)\\mathbf{i}+\\ln 2\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\cos 1\\,\\mathbf{k}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707889}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "41b4faa0-b9de-5bf2-9692-bd3f0ea6f9e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(\\arctan 2+\\frac{2}{5}\\right)\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{j}+\\cos 1\\,\\mathbf{k}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707878} :answer-field/id #uuid "58eccd43-338d-549e-9df2-f2bd0baacae7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707881}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "eaae687d-c8cf-59cf-bdb7-6fe36f7d5294" :question/problem "Find $\\mathbf{f}\\prime(1)$ for\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{f}(t)=t\\arctan(2t)\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\ln(t+1)\\,\\mathbf{j}+(\\cos t+t\\sin t)\\,\\mathbf{k}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Differentiate each scalar component, keeping the basis vectors fixed. The first component needs the product rule and the chain rule:\n\n$$\n\\frac{d}{dt}\\bigl(t\\arctan(2t)\\bigr)=\\arctan(2t)+\\frac{2t}{1+4t^2}.\n$$\n\nFor the other two components,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{d}{dt}\\ln(t+1)&=\\frac{1}{t+1}, \\\\\n\\frac{d}{dt}(\\cos t+t\\sin t)&=-\\sin t+\\sin t+t\\cos t=t\\cos t.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{f}\\prime(t)=\\left(\\arctan(2t)+\\frac{2t}{1+4t^2}\\right)\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{1}{t+1}\\mathbf{j}+t\\cos t\\,\\mathbf{k}.\n$$\n\nSubstitute $t=1$ only after differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{f}\\prime(1)=\\left(\\arctan 2+\\frac{2}{5}\\right)\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{j}+\\cos 1\\,\\mathbf{k}.\n$$\n\nThe angles are in radians; $\\arctan 2$ and $\\cos 1$ remain exact values."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708316 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9b186955-ef0c-5702-9ddb-583bea9a5221" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 6 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708338}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b186955-ef0c-5702-9ddb-583bea9a5221" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 6 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708338} :answer-field/id #uuid "571e3883-c61a-5b1f-a913-a2cb01a1ac84" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708325} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24fbec10-5623-5867-ba22-1ed6ead58a63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{\\sqrt{1 + \\pi^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708317}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "24fbec10-5623-5867-ba22-1ed6ead58a63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{\\sqrt{1 + \\pi^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708317} :answer-field/id #uuid "80fe441c-8fa4-58b8-9702-dd7f941f1cf5" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708333} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "68098fb1-fd82-5430-9779-c8b685dcaa72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708330}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "68098fb1-fd82-5430-9779-c8b685dcaa72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708330} :answer-field/id #uuid "d56ff1f8-0485-58de-9dea-74ee80c2cf14" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708341}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2350fa1f-4d61-508f-a687-c7e028222e19" :question/problem "Find $\\mathbf{f}'(\\pi)$ for\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{f}(t)&=\\left(- 3 t^{2}\\right)\\mathbf{i} \\\\ &+\\left(2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\mathbf{j} \\\\ &+\\left(\\sqrt{t^{2} + 1}\\right)\\mathbf{k}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEnter exact components in order.\n\n$\\mathbf{f}'(\\pi)=\\langle$ {{field-1}} $,$ {{field-2}} $,$ {{field-3}} $\\rangle$" :question/worked-solution "Let $f_1$, $f_2$, and $f_3$ be the components in the given order. Differentiate each scalar component separately.\n\nFor component 1, use the power and chain rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_{1}'(t)&=\\frac{d}{dt}\\left(- 3 t^{2}\\right) \\\\ &=- 6 t\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor component 2, use the trigonometric and chain rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_{2}'(t)&=\\frac{d}{dt}\\left(2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) \\\\ &=2\\cdot 1\\cdot - \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\\\ &=- 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor component 3, use the square-root and chain rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_{3}'(t)&=\\frac{d}{dt}\\left(\\sqrt{t^{2} + 1}\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{t^{2} + 1}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{f}'(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}- 6 t \\\\ - 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\\\ \\frac{t}{\\sqrt{t^{2} + 1}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSubstitute $t=\\pi$ into the derivative, after differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_{1}'(\\pi)&=- 6 \\left(\\pi\\right) \\\\ &=- 6 \\pi \\\\ f_{2}'(\\pi)&=- 2 \\sin{\\left(\\left(\\pi\\right) \\right)} \\\\ &=0 \\\\ f_{3}'(\\pi)&=\\frac{\\left(\\pi\\right)}{\\sqrt{\\left(\\pi\\right)^{2} + 1}} \\\\ &=\\frac{\\pi}{\\sqrt{1 + \\pi^{2}}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nKeeping the component order gives\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{f}'(\\pi)=\\begin{bmatrix}- 6 \\pi \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{\\pi}{\\sqrt{1 + \\pi^{2}}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708326 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "99c5f964-054a-5546-9c4c-d503abb5bc5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{2 \\sqrt{1 + \\frac{\\pi^{2}}{4}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708337}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "99c5f964-054a-5546-9c4c-d503abb5bc5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{2 \\sqrt{1 + \\frac{\\pi^{2}}{4}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708337} :answer-field/id #uuid "417bf7a1-f108-5304-a6bb-78818d60f668" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708319} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5fbbdcab-52e1-5ef5-9dc0-b3cce5f98e10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708328}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5fbbdcab-52e1-5ef5-9dc0-b3cce5f98e10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708328} :answer-field/id #uuid "8104251d-d64a-5610-a456-77606871b1d1" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708334} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14f5b812-bdc3-5ddd-b70e-20bca05269f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi + 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708315}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "14f5b812-bdc3-5ddd-b70e-20bca05269f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi + 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708315} :answer-field/id #uuid "d757151d-ed30-5905-8b56-6e41b3219678" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708342}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5afa5028-7eb7-5d8d-9d22-4bdf892ac163" :question/problem "Find $\\mathbf{f}'\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)$ for\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{f}(t)=\\left\\langle \\sqrt{t^{2} + 1},\\,\\left(t + 2\\right)^{2},\\,2 \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right\\rangle.\n$$\n\nEnter exact components in order.\n\n$\\mathbf{f}'\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)=\\langle$ {{field-1}} $,$ {{field-2}} $,$ {{field-3}} $\\rangle$" :question/worked-solution "Let $f_1$, $f_2$, and $f_3$ be the components in the given order. Differentiate each scalar component separately.\n\nFor component 1, use the square-root and chain rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_{1}'(t)&=\\frac{d}{dt}\\left(\\sqrt{t^{2} + 1}\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{t^{2} + 1}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor component 2, use the power and chain rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_{2}'(t)&=\\frac{d}{dt}\\left(\\left(t + 2\\right)^{2}\\right) \\\\ &=2 t + 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor component 3, use the trigonometric and chain rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_{3}'(t)&=\\frac{d}{dt}\\left(2 \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right) \\\\ &=2\\cdot 2\\cdot - \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)} \\\\ &=- 4 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{f}'(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{t^{2} + 1}} \\\\ 2 t + 4 \\\\ - 4 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSubstitute $t=\\frac{\\pi}{2}$ into the derivative, after differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_{1}'\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)&=\\frac{\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)}{\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)^{2} + 1}} \\\\ &=\\frac{\\pi}{2 \\sqrt{1 + \\frac{\\pi^{2}}{4}}} \\\\ f_{2}'\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)&=2 \\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right) + 4 \\\\ &=\\pi + 4 \\\\ f_{3}'\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)&=- 4 \\sin{\\left(2 \\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right) \\right)} \\\\ &=0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nKeeping the component order gives\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{f}'\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{\\pi}{2 \\sqrt{1 + \\frac{\\pi^{2}}{4}}} \\\\ \\pi + 4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708336 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6778b0d6-5888-572a-870b-5f14fd100121" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708329}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6778b0d6-5888-572a-870b-5f14fd100121" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708329} :answer-field/id #uuid "36a13c3b-4e5a-5957-a1b9-22c86136f896" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708318} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87fbcd24-a8c3-5efe-9c46-237ad72cf479" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708335}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87fbcd24-a8c3-5efe-9c46-237ad72cf479" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708335} :answer-field/id #uuid "448fa99b-c053-5a1c-9329-082479c8bfdf" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708321} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43f3ed21-b0ec-550c-a79d-d8a4b133044b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708320}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43f3ed21-b0ec-550c-a79d-d8a4b133044b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708320} :answer-field/id #uuid "d12c77cc-4ce8-5707-8809-70205dccd528" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708340}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8d0e2560-8cf3-55fa-b25d-6fed230792be" :question/problem "Find $\\mathbf{f}'(\\pi)$ for\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{f}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 t^{2} \\\\ 2 t - \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\\\ - \\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nEnter exact components in order.\n\n$\\mathbf{f}'(\\pi)=\\langle$ {{field-1}} $,$ {{field-2}} $,$ {{field-3}} $\\rangle$" :question/worked-solution "Let $f_1$, $f_2$, and $f_3$ be the components in the given order. Differentiate each scalar component separately.\n\nFor component 1, use the power and sum rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_{1}'(t)&=\\frac{d}{dt}\\left(2 t^{2}\\right) \\\\ &=4 t\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor component 2, use the trigonometric, sum and power rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_{2}'(t)&=\\frac{d}{dt}\\left(2 t - \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) \\\\ &=2 - \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor component 3, use the trigonometric and chain rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_{3}'(t)&=\\frac{d}{dt}\\left(- \\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\right) \\\\ &=-1\\cdot 3\\cdot - \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)} \\\\ &=3 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{f}'(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}4 t \\\\ 2 - \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} \\\\ 3 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSubstitute $t=\\pi$ into the derivative, after differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_{1}'(\\pi)&=4 \\left(\\pi\\right) \\\\ &=4 \\pi \\\\ f_{2}'(\\pi)&=2 - \\cos{\\left(\\left(\\pi\\right) \\right)} \\\\ &=3 \\\\ f_{3}'(\\pi)&=3 \\sin{\\left(3 \\left(\\pi\\right) \\right)} \\\\ &=0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nKeeping the component order gives\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{f}'(\\pi)=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\pi \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708339 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08770cfb-fba6-50dd-9584-e98ea8844ded" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 3 e^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708312}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08770cfb-fba6-50dd-9584-e98ea8844ded" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 3 e^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708312} :answer-field/id #uuid "12640ad6-d6c2-5ca2-93ba-21aa729c51f7" :answer-field/key "fie